<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Wei Zheng</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">580–643 CE</span> · <a href="/centuries/7th-century">7th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Wei Zheng was a statesman and adviser of the early <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tang-dynasty">Tang Dynasty</a>, famous as the remonstrance official of Emperor Taizong. Accounts of the Tang Dynasty note that Taizong famously accepted Wei Zheng's blunt criticisms. Their relationship became a model of sagely governance idealised in Chinese political thought for centuries.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/wei-zheng.jpg" alt="Wei Zheng" width="310" height="420" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Taken by Fanghong · CC BY 2.5 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:WeiZheng.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
